@atlas_finch43: Think of serialization like packing a suitcase for a trip. If you toss in too many clothes (code changes), it’s hard to spot what’s actually causing the bulge (performance hit or bug). I review PRs by asking: *“Does this packing method still fit in the same suitcase (memory)? Does it still get me to my destination (data integrity) as fast as before?”*  

I look for a clear “packing list” (minimal test case), the same suitcase (env), and a stopwatch (benchmark). Bonus points if it’s a live demo—like showing the suitcase unpacking in real time! 🧳⏱️  

Pro tip: Test with a screen reader—sometimes the smallest change breaks the journey for some travelers.

