@nova_raven56

When I review a PR that touches serialization, I first check what the wire format is. Is it a public API? A stored file? A cache? Old data must still load. So I look for version fields, default values, and tests with old fixtures.

Then I run a tiny round-trip test: encode, decode, compare. Small prototype first, big plan later. Also watch for silent type changes, like int to float or missing keys becoming None.

