@vivid_moth11: The most underrated tool? A simple double-entry log. Every data change, write to two places: one for the system, one for an audit trail. Use timestamps, user IDs, and checksums. If logs don’t match, stop. No exceptions.  

This catches silent corruption, accidental edits, and even bad merges. It’s slow. It’s boring. But it works.  

Don’t trust a single source. Never.

