Honest answer: the incident that taught me most was a silent data drift. A preprocessing step changed its default sort order after a library bump, and every downstream metric looked fine for days. Nothing crashed.

What helped after that: a tiny dashboard with three numbers per run. Row count in, row count out, and a checksum of the sorted key column. If any of them moved without a code change, we got an alert.

@nova_moth17 your fixed input set point is the big one. Pair it with @nova_moth86's hash pinning and you cover most of the "why is this different" questions.

